BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:All Church Camping Weekend at Reunion Flat
DTSTART;TZID=America/Denver:20260828T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Denver:20260828T170000
UID:5dac2352f10d42a72e59f9ea7719f98e@churchinthetetons.org
DESCRIPTION:Under the Canopy of God’s Creation – CiT Outdoor Retreat S
 ignup Here Where : Reunion Flats Campground Site B. When : Friday August 2
 8th-Sunday August 30th: campers can check in after 2pm on the 28th\, and e
 veryone must be checked out by noon on the 30th. Shared meal : Saturday Au
 g 29th\, 5:30PM\, Nacho Bar\, there will be paper sign ups to attend and b
 ring food every Sunday at church and electronically on the CiT website\, M
 inistry of Fun will provide paper products\, water and lemonade\, and set 
 up gas camp stoves and hopefully fire in the fire ring if permitted at tha
 t time. Vespers (evening service) Saturday Aug. 29th\, 7P: devotional and 
 music to give thanks to God for all his glory and creation. Immediately fo
 llowing there will be a dessert contest\, asking everyone to bring their b
 est smores creations. Sunday 30th: bagels\, fruit and coffee provided for 
 those who are camping\, it’s service Sunday\, so those at the campground
  will be sent off to projects in prayer by AJ. There will be at least 1 se
 rvice project in Reunion Flats. The Mission Team will be providing service
  project ideas/signups closer to the weekend. Directions: Head east out of
  Driggs on E. Ski Hill Road toward Alta\, WY. Turn right onto Forest Road 
 009 and go 3 miles to the campground. The last 2 miles of the drive is a g
 ravel road and easily drivable in any type of car. We will put up signs al
 ong the route for easy wayfinding. Parking: there is ample parking at the 
 site\, enough for 12 cars/trucks\, and overflow parking is a short walk/sh
 uttle to Treasure Lake Area. We will make sure everyone has a place to par
 k and shuttle anyone as needed. Good things to know: There are lots of spo
 ts to tent camp on this site. Again\, helpful if groups/individuals campin
 g\, sign up on paper or website. We can also make room for small hard side
 d campers. If someone wishes to bring one\,please sign up. It is primitive
  camping\, no hookups. There is potable water for cooking and washing\, bu
 t we recommend you bring water to stay hydrated. There are 2 picnic tables
  we can dine on\, and camp chairs would be good to bring. This is the most
  shaded area of this campground and we will set up a canopy/shade shelter 
 as well. There are lots of hikes\, streams\, fishing spots\, biking trails
  in the area. More info to come about a possible guided hike for all\, and
  treasure hunt for kids. Save the Date Learn More
LOCATION:Church in the Tetons\, 60 South Main St\, Driggs\, ID 83422
URL:https://www.churchinthetetons.org/events/all-church-camping-weekend-at
 -reunion-flat/
X-SOURCE:Church in the Tetons
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
